WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:17.704
Dr. Dolittle and his friends stayed on Spider Monkey Island for over a month.

2
00:00:18.404 --> 00:00:19.865
During that time, Dr.

3
00:00:19.905 --> 00:00:23.286
Dolittle and Long Arrow spent many days learning from each other.

4
00:00:24.046 --> 00:00:26.787
Long Arrow taught the doctor about herbs and plants.

5
00:00:26.807 --> 00:00:31.248
"Do not touch the leaves on this one," the Indian said in eagle talk.

6
00:00:31.888 --> 00:00:35.330
"Only pick it by its stem."

7
00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.192
Dr. Dolittle taught Long Arrow about modern medicine.

8
00:00:38.212 --> 00:00:41.134
"Put this in your ears," he said.

9
00:00:41.754 --> 00:00:45.336
The doctor held up a stethoscope and passed it to the Indian.

10
00:00:45.936 --> 00:00:48.658
He held the metal disc against Long Arrow's chest.

11
00:00:49.318 --> 00:00:51.300
Long Arrow jumped back in fear.

12
00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:55.262
"Don't worry," laughed Dr.

13
00:00:55.302 --> 00:00:58.344
Dolittle. "That's the sound of your heart beating."

14
00:01:00.868 --> 00:01:05.011
As the days went by, Tommy noticed it getting colder and colder.

15
00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.352
"Brrrr," he shivered.

16
00:01:07.372 --> 00:01:09.133
"It feels like winter."

17
00:01:09.153 --> 00:01:13.175
"Yes, I noticed that, too," the doctor remarked.

18
00:01:13.816 --> 00:01:16.017
He looked around the village of Popsipetal.

19
00:01:16.557 --> 00:01:20.359
People everywhere seemed to be trembling and shaking from the cold.

20
00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:24.622
Dr. Dolittle and Tommy walked to the beach.

21
00:01:25.282 --> 00:01:28.384
They saw a large flock of birds shivering in the cold.

22
00:01:29.024 --> 00:01:30.044
"Dr. Dolittle!"

23
00:01:30.264 --> 00:01:31.485
called out Polynesia.

24
00:01:32.145 --> 00:01:35.766
Tommy noticed that her beak was blue and her wings were shaking.

25
00:01:35.786 --> 00:01:38.847
"What's going on here, Polynesia?"

26
00:01:39.147 --> 00:01:40.387
the doctor looked around.

27
00:01:40.407 --> 00:01:44.428
"They're all leaving," she replied, pointing to the birds.

28
00:01:44.448 --> 00:01:46.829
"It's too cold for them to live here."

29
00:01:46.849 --> 00:01:49.650
"But what is causing this sudden cold?"

30
00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:51.230
the doctor asked aloud.

31
00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:54.491
"It's the island, Doctor," answered the parrot.

32
00:01:55.031 --> 00:01:57.692
"Spider Monkey Island is a floating island."

33
00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.902
Dr. Dolittle slapped his knee.

34
00:02:00.922 --> 00:02:02.783
"That's right!

35
00:02:03.284 --> 00:02:04.985
So we must be moving south."

36
00:02:05.666 --> 00:02:07.627
"Are we moving toward the South Pole?"

37
00:02:07.948 --> 00:02:08.949
asked Polynesia.

38
00:02:08.969 --> 00:02:12.351
"It seems that way," the doctor answered.

39
00:02:12.371 --> 00:02:15.955
"We must turn around, Doctor," said Tommy urgently.

40
00:02:15.975 --> 00:02:20.659
"The Popsipetal people and the animals can't survive in a cold climate."

41
00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:26.584
As soon as Tommy had spoken, all the animals started to come out of the forest.

42
00:02:27.176 --> 00:02:32.518
There were monkeys, opossums, butterflies, pigs, and all kinds of insects.

43
00:02:32.538 --> 00:02:34.658
"Please help us, Dr.

44
00:02:34.678 --> 00:02:36.479
Dolittle," said one monkey.

45
00:02:36.499 --> 00:02:39.159
"We're all so cold."

46
00:02:39.179 --> 00:02:43.721
"All the plants and fruits are freezing," cried an opossum.

47
00:02:43.741 --> 00:02:45.901
"There is nothing to eat."

48
00:02:46.922 --> 00:02:49.802
Dr. Dolittle thought and thought about what he could do.

49
00:02:49.822 --> 00:02:54.864
"Polynesia," he said finally, "we need the help of some whales."

50
00:02:55.604 --> 00:02:57.104
"Whales?" asked Tommy.

51
00:02:57.124 --> 00:03:02.026
"Whales are big strong creatures," explained the doctor.

52
00:03:02.046 --> 00:03:05.467
"Perhaps they can push the island back north."

53
00:03:06.027 --> 00:03:09.868
So Polynesia and some other birds flew off in search of whales.

54
00:03:10.668 --> 00:03:13.709
Shortly, Polynesia returned with two dolphins.

55
00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:19.231
"I asked for whales, Polynesia," sighed the doctor.

56
00:03:19.251 --> 00:03:21.531
"Not to worry, Dr.

57
00:03:21.551 --> 00:03:23.212
Dolittle," said one dolphin.

58
00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.662
"The whales are already in the back pushing you along."

59
00:03:26.682 --> 00:03:29.523
"But I can't feel anything," said Tommy.

60
00:03:30.364 --> 00:03:32.665
The dolphins stared at him with open mouths.

61
00:03:32.685 --> 00:03:34.926
"He can speak our language, too?"

62
00:03:35.327 --> 00:03:35.907
they cried.

63
00:03:35.927 --> 00:03:40.770
"Yes, he's very clever," the doctor said proudly.

64
00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:43.531
"Now, how many whales are there?"

65
00:03:43.551 --> 00:03:48.454
"We were lucky, and ran into a large herd," replied Polynesia.

66
00:03:48.474 --> 00:03:51.676
"Good work, Polynesia," smiled the doctor.

67
00:03:52.296 --> 00:03:54.358
"We should soon be heading back north."

68
00:03:55.219 --> 00:03:58.561
All the animals, birds, and other creatures cheered loudly.

69
00:04:00.223 --> 00:04:04.646
Tommy wanted to ask the dolphins, "Why does this island float?"

70
00:04:05.307 --> 00:04:11.031
But he made a mistake in dolphin language and said instead, "Do your toes float in water?"

71
00:04:11.732 --> 00:04:15.715
Dr. Dolittle, Polynesia, and the dolphins could not stop laughing.

72
00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:18.217
Poor Tommy turned bright red.

73
00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:21.140
He asked again, correctly this time.

74
00:04:23.272 --> 00:04:29.737
A big dolphin explained: "Spider Monkey Island used to be a part of a large piece of land.

75
00:04:30.358 --> 00:04:34.101
But for some reason it broke away and fell into the water.

76
00:04:34.521 --> 00:04:36.803
Only part of the island is above the water.

77
00:04:37.163 --> 00:04:39.265
The other, bigger half is underwater."

78
00:04:40.606 --> 00:04:44.089
Another dolphin continued: "See all those mountains.

79
00:04:44.889 --> 00:04:47.632
For some strange reason, they are hollow.

80
00:04:48.432 --> 00:04:52.776
When the land fell into the water, the air inside stopped it from sinking.

81
00:04:53.472 --> 00:04:55.153
That is why the island floats."

82
00:04:55.173 --> 00:04:58.075
"Just like a balloon," Tommy exclaimed.

83
00:04:58.095 --> 00:05:03.758
"There must be a way to stop the island from floating," said Dr.

84
00:05:03.798 --> 00:05:08.540
Dolittle. "We need to get the air out of the mountains," said Polynesia.

85
00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:09.761
"But how?"

86
00:05:10.081 --> 00:05:10.661
asked Tommy.

87
00:05:11.422 --> 00:05:14.744
Everyone thought, but no one could come up with a solution.
